# 行尾唯一权威：仓库内存 LF，检出亦 LF。
#
# WHY this file exists (measured 2026-10-16):
#   `git ls-files --eol` over the whole repo: 1821 blobs are i/lf, ZERO are i/crlf
#   (the two `i/` entries are gitlinks: Aegis, dsh-taskboard). But the *working
#   tree* under scripts/ splits three ways by file provenance: 89 w/crlf, 86 w/lf,
#   3 w/mixed. Nothing in the repo decides that -- it falls out of whatever
#   `core.autocrlf` each developer happens to have set (this host: true) and
#   whether a file arrived by `git checkout` (converted) or was written by a tool
#   (left LF).
#
# The consequence is not cosmetic. Three governance shells were checked out as
# CRLF -- check_cli_startup.sh, check_doc_drift.sh, check_lock_await.sh -- so the
# documented local command `bash scripts/check_doc_drift.sh` dies on `$'\r':
# command not found` while the identical CI run on Linux passes, because CI checks
# out the LF blob. A "local-only" failure that CI cannot see is the worst kind of
# reproducibility defect, and this repo has already been bitten repeatedly by
# line-ending-sensitive anchors silently matching zero bytes (see the CLAIM
# reasoning in scripts/gate_manifest.toml G-119 and the fixture assertions in
# scripts/check_l0_logic_ledger.py --selftest, which has to write every fixture
# twice, once LF and once CRLF, to prove its parser is eol-independent).
#
# Scope is the audited governance surface, on purpose:
#   * /scripts/**  -- the 91 .py + ledgers (.txt) + gate_manifest.toml + .sh/.ps1.
#                     Every blob there is already LF, so this line cannot trigger a
#                     renormalisation storm; it only removes the smudge conversion.
#   * *.sh anywhere -- a CRLF shell script is broken on Linux by definition.
#
# Deliberately NOT declared here: *.ps1 outside scripts/ (PowerShell tolerates
# either, and scripts/ .ps1 files are already covered), and any file that stores
# line endings as DATA. If such a fixture is ever added, mark it `-text` explicitly
# rather than loosening these rules.
#
# Follow-up that this file does NOT perform: `git add --renormalize .` would also
# rewrite the 89 CRLF working copies in one sweep. That is a separate, deliberate,
# all-or-nothing act -- it is intentionally left to a human signing a commit.

/scripts/** text eol=lf
*.sh      text eol=lf
